    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "> This does mean that if you forget the indexName, there's no warning, no error, and no rendering. Maybe there should be a warning or error if there are no child widgets that will be rendered (not sure if it's possible though)?\r\n\r\nIf the goal is to prevent firing requests to Algolia with no index at all, would it be possible to have a `noIndexNameWarning` flag set to `true` initially that gets changed to `false`:\r\n- if the index name is set in InstantSearch parameters\r\n- when addWidgets is called with a child index\r\n\r\nThis might be a bit overengineered though. Wdyt?",
    "commit_id": "0c09c2e019bca50885e3dab02424924163c16c70",
